From b25a39be55c83be392c8b5ea5fd926a4dad14f33 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 23:12:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/21] feat(offers): what a member is open to, saved from the
 chat (1698, A15)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

D679/D680. A member's needs are stored (every goal is one), but what he is
OPEN TO („if anyone needs hospitality in Adjara, I'm interested") had nowhere
to live once automatic answers were switched off (D669). It is the strongest
willingness signal there is.

Migration 223 adds the offers table (user, one line, field, active, source).
offers.service saves (at most 20 active), lists the owner's own, and switches
one off on „forget that". The row stays for the admin per-user page, the
only other place it shows. Three tools, save_offer / list_offers /
delete_offer, are gated on the server: owner's own run only, and save only
with confirmed: true.

HELD BEHIND A SWITCH: OFFER_TOOLS_ON is false, so no run is given the tools
until Misho approves their texts (§109, D44, NIGHT_QUESTIONS AM). With the
switch off, this commit changes nothing a model or a person sees, so it can
ship.

DONE WHEN (after the switch): a seat says „if anyone needs hospitality in
Adjara, I'm interested", the assistant confirms one line, and an offers row
exists with the field; „forget that" switches it off; the row shows only on
the owner's own request and the admin page.

